            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="LAW03" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Sir</roleName>
                        <forename>William</forename>
                        <surname>Lawrence</surname>
                        <addName>baronet</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1783-07-16">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1867-07-05"/>
                    <occupation>surgeon</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>There are a number of Lawrences identified in the diary.  The main discussion 
    of the different individuals involved is in the entry for <persName key="LAW01">Thomas Lawrence</persName></p>
                        <p>Sir William Lawrence was a surgeon, and from 1815 Professor of anatomy and surgery at the 
      Royal College of Surgeons in London.  He was consulted both by <persName key="SHE02">Mary Shelley</persName> (in 1814) and 
      <persName key="SHE01">Percy Bysshe Shelley</persName> in 1815.  Godwin first notes 'Lawrence, surgeon' in his diary in 1812.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">St Clair</bibl>
